{
  "hooks": {
    "InstructionsLoaded": [
      {
        "matcher": "",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/validate-instructions.sh",
            "args": []
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/protect-files.sh",
            "args": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "prompt",
            "prompt": "You are a Go architecture import matrix enforcer.\n\nRULES (strict, zero exceptions):\n1. handler layer (internal/handler/) may import: service, controller, models. NEVER: repository\n2. service layer (internal/service/) may import: repository, models. NEVER: handler\n3. repository layer (internal/repository/) may import: models. NEVER: handler, service\n4. models layer (internal/models/) stdlib only. NEVER: any internal/ package\n\nAnalyze this tool call for import violations:\n\n$ARGUMENTS\n\nSTEPS:\n1. Extract file_path from tool_input to determine the layer (handler/service/repository/models)\n2. If file is not in one of the 4 layers, respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"allow\"}\n3. If file is a test file (*_test.go), respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"allow\"}\n4. Find import statements in tool_input.content (Write) or tool_input.new_string (Edit)\n5. If no import statements found, respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"allow\"}\n6. Check each internal/ import against the rules for that layer\n7. If violation found, respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"deny\", \"permissionDecisionReason\": \"Import violation: [layer] must not import [forbidden package]\"}\n8. If no violations, respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"allow\"}\n\nRespond with ONLY the JSON object, nothing else.",
            "if": "Write(internal/**/*.go)",
            "timeout": 30
          },
          {
            "type": "prompt",
            "prompt": "You are a Go architecture import matrix enforcer.\n\nRULES (strict, zero exceptions):\n1. handler layer (internal/handler/) may import: service, controller, models. NEVER: repository\n2. service layer (internal/service/) may import: repository, models. NEVER: handler\n3. repository layer (internal/repository/) may import: models. NEVER: handler, service\n4. models layer (internal/models/) stdlib only. NEVER: any internal/ package\n\nAnalyze this tool call for import violations:\n\n$ARGUMENTS\n\nSTEPS:\n1. Extract file_path from tool_input to determine the layer (handler/service/repository/models)\n2. If file is not in one of the 4 layers, respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"allow\"}\n3. If file is a test file (*_test.go), respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"allow\"}\n4. Find import statements in tool_input.content (Write) or tool_input.new_string (Edit)\n5. If no import statements found, respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"allow\"}\n6. Check each internal/ import against the rules for that layer\n7. If violation found, respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"deny\", \"permissionDecisionReason\": \"Import violation: [layer] must not import [forbidden package]\"}\n8. If no violations, respond {\"permissionDecision\": \"allow\"}\n\nRespond with ONLY the JSON object, nothing else.",
            "if": "Edit(internal/**/*.go)",
            "timeout": 30
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-artifact-size.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Write(.claude/**)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/pre-commit-build.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Bash(git commit*)"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/auto-fmt.sh",
            "args": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/yaml-lint.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Edit(.claude/**)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-references.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Write(.claude/**)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-references.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Edit(.claude/**)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-references.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Write(README.md)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-references.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Edit(README.md)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-references.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Write(CLAUDE.md)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-references.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Edit(CLAUDE.md)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-references.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Write(install.sh)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-references.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Edit(install.sh)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-plan-drift.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Write(.claude/**)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/agents/meta-agent/scripts/check-plan-drift.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Edit(.claude/**)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/validate-handoff.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Write(.claude/workflow-state/*-handoff.json)"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/validate-handoff.sh",
            "args": [],
            "if": "Edit(.claude/workflow-state/*-handoff.json)"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "matcher": "manual",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/save-progress-before-compact.sh",
            "args": []
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "auto",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.claude/scripts/save-progress-before-compact.sh",
            "args": []
